  "worked_solution": "Since the cosine of an angle equals the sine of its complement, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{57}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({90}^{∘}-{57}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence, $x={33}^{∘}$ satisfies the given equation.",
